    "pathway_role_summary": "GSK3B is a central regulatory kinase in the beta-catenin destruction complex of the canonical Wnt signaling pathway. In the absence of Wnt ligands, GSK3B phosphorylates beta-catenin at Ser33/Ser37/Thr41, marking it for ubiquitin-mediated proteasomal degradation. Upon Wnt activation, GSK3B is inhibited, allowing beta-catenin accumulation and transcriptional activation. GSK3B also regulates insulin signaling by phosphorylating and inhibiting glycogen synthase, playing a critical role in glucose homeostasis. Additionally involved in Alzheimer's disease pathology through tau phosphorylation."
  },
