    "data_quality_notes": "High quality data with extensive experimental validation. Over 140 PDB structures available. Some InterPro/PROSITE entries accessed indirectly through literature due to web interface limitations. Isoform 2 sequence not fully detailed in available sources. PTM sites well-characterized. Interaction data highly confident with multiple independent validations.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "GSK3B is a critical node in the beta-catenin destruction complex, directly phosphorylating beta-catenin to regulate its stability. Key regulatory phosphorylation sites (Ser9 inactivating, Tyr216 activating) control kinase activity. Essential for modeling Wnt pathway dynamics, APC tumor suppressor function, and beta-catenin-dependent transcription. Well-characterized substrate specificity (primed phosphorylation at P+4) and extensive structural data enable detailed mechanistic modeling of destruction complex assembly and activity."
